# The World Atlas, first region.
#
# Eight nodes, 51 essence to unlock everything. Clearing all twenty shipped levels once pays at least
# 77 — one essence per base score harvested — so the whole region is reachable by playing the campaign,
# with Endless Wayfare as a top-up rather than a requirement. The gate in AtlasPackTests checks that
# relationship, so a node made dearer than the game can pay for fails CI.
#
# Effects are additive on every board, and deliberately small: three skips and three tokens at full
# unlock, against the three skips a level already grants. A relic should ease a board, not answer it.

pack: biome1

# The root, and the cheapest thing in the region: somewhere to start.
node: spring-well cost 3 at 0,0 gives skip 1

# The two directions the region opens into — one buys room to manoeuvre, the other buys a mistake back.
node: deep-channel cost 5 at 1,0 gives token 1 needs spring-well
node: ley-line cost 4 at 0,1 gives essence 1 needs spring-well

# Second ring.
node: tide-lens cost 6 at 2,0 gives skip 1 needs deep-channel
node: crystal-facet cost 6 at 0,2 gives token 1 needs ley-line

# The join: a node reachable only by going both ways first, which is what a non-linear map is for.
node: glass-siphon cost 8 at 1,1 gives essence 1 needs deep-channel,ley-line

# Outer edge. A second region docks here by naming these in its own docks line.
node: storm-eye cost 9 at 2,1 gives skip 1 needs tide-lens
node: wayfarer-mark cost 10 at 1,2 gives token 1 needs glass-siphon,crystal-facet
